    "wikipedia:en": {
      "qid": "Q55561",
      "lang": "en",
      "title": "3D Construction Kit",
      "extract": "3D Construction Kit (US, Canada and Israel release title: Virtual Reality Studio), also known as 3D Virtual Studio, is a utility for creating 3D worlds in Freescape. Developed by Incentive Software and published by Domark, it was released in 1991 on multiple platforms. The game originally retailed for £24.99 for the 8-bit version, and £49.99 for 16-bit version and the 32-bit Acorn Archimedes version, in the United Kingdom. A sequel, 3D Construction Kit II, was released in 1992, but only available on Amiga, Atari ST and MS-DOS.",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/3D_Construction_Kit"
    },
    "wikipedia:es": {
      "qid": "Q55561",
      "lang": "es",
      "title": "3D Construction Kit",
      "extract": "3D Construction Kit (publicado en EE. UU., Canadá e Israel con el título: Virtual Reality Studio​), también conocido como 3D Virtual Studio, es una utilidad para crear mundos 3D en Freescape. Desarrollado por Incentive Software y comercializado por Domark, fue publicado en 1991 para múltiples plataformas. El año siguiente se publicó una secuela.",
      "url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/3D_Construction_Kit"
